        "jsCode": "// Fires once when the loop finishes — emits a single summary item.\n// Wire this to Slack/Telegram/Email later if you want a heartbeat per run.\nconst all = $input.all();\nconst counts = all.reduce((a, it) => {\n  const c = it.json.category || 'UNKNOWN';\n  a[c] = (a[c] || 0) + 1;\n  return a;\n}, {});\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    run_completed_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n    total: all.length,\n    by_category: counts\n  }\n}];"
